        "question-1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What are Rectified Tiles?",
            "answer": "<p>Rectified tiles are ceramic or porcelain tiles that are made to a precise tolerance. This means they are cut to near exact measurements with a near perfect straight edge.  <a href=\"/pages/what-are-rectified-tiles\" title=\"What are rectified tiles?\">Read More</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "question-2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the difference between porcelain and ceramic tiles?",
            "answer": "<p>Porcelain tiles use a more refined clay and are fired at higher temperatures. This makes porcelain tiles denser and more durable. Porcelain tiles are considered to be a higher quality than ceramic tiles. <a href=\"/pages/what-is-the-difference-between-porcelain-and-ceramic-tiles\" title=\"What is the difference between porcelain and ceramic tiles?\">Read More.</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "question-3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can all tiles be used on walls and floors?",
            "answer": "<p>The simple answer to this no. Walls tiles are not suitable for use on a floor. However many tiles are multi-use for walls and floors. You just need to check they are suitable for use on a floor, then they can be used on walls <a href=\"/pages/can-all-tiles-be-used-on-walls-and-floors\" title=\"Can all tiles be used on walls and floors?\">Read More.</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "68768913-de08-48d1-a24c-cec67acbfdd1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What tiles should I use in a wet room?",
            "answer": "<p>Careful consideration should be given when choosing tiles for a wet room. With the floor of a wet room being used like a shower tray, it is important to think about how slippery the floor could get. With this in mind we recommend that the tiles for the floor of a wet room should have a high anti slip rating. <a href=\"/pages/what-tiles-should-i-use-in-a-wet-room\" title=\"What tiles should I use in a wet room?\">Read More.</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "059ae8dc-a7f7-4755-bcf6-d69241385b75": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What tiles are suitable for underfloor heating?",
            "answer": "<p>Choosing to install underfloor heating does not diminish the choice of floor tiles you can use. As with all floor tiles, using textured floor tiles will give you more grip, especially if the floor is likely to get wet. <a href=\"/pages/what-tiles-are-suitable-for-underfloor-heating\" title=\"What tiles are suitable for underfloor heating?\">Read More.</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "48052b8a-1fbf-422a-92af-b93594a37e65": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the maximum weight restriction for wall tiling?",
            "answer": "<p>Over recent years there has been high demand for larger and larger tiles. With this in mind it is important to take into consideration the weight of any tiles you are installing on your walls. Remember you need to consider the weight of any adhesive used as well as the tiles. <a href=\"/pages/what-is-the-maximum-weight-restriction-for-wall-tiling\" title=\"What is the maximum weight restriction for wall tiling?\">Read More.</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "25b87c5c-99e4-485a-931b-1aed7b116772": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is shade variation and how can I avoid it?",
            "answer": "<p>Over recent years there has been high demand for larger and larger tiles. With this in mind it is important to take into consideration the weight of any tiles you are installing on your walls. Remember you need to consider the weight of any adhesive used as well as the tiles. <a href=\"/pages/what-is-shade-variation-and-how-can-i-avoid-it\" title=\"What is shade variation and how can I avoid it?\">Read More.</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "b79d56ce-7b67-4619-9b61-2307408e7030": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What tiles are best for using outdoors?",
            "answer": "<p>Matt porcelain tiles are the best choice for tiling outdoors. Porcelain tiles with a textured surface will also help stop the tiles becoming slippery when wet. Natural stone tiles such as granite, slate and travertine can also be used externally. <a href=\"/pages/what-tiles-are-best-for-using-outdoors\" title=\"What tiles are best for using outdoors?\">Read More.</a></p>"
          }
        },
